# promise: #714
# ⌥← / ⌥→ typed on the keyboard are the page's, as in Arc, Chrome and Safari: YouTube's previous and next chapter,
# a word in a text field. Since #233 Cra took them over a page for Back and Forward, so a YouTube video left its
# page. The keys a mouse driver posts for a side button (Logi Options+ types ⌥← / ⌥→) still go back and forward.
# The keys go through the app's event queue, where Cra's key monitor decides; the decision is
# OptionArrowsOnThePageTests (and MouseButtonSpaceSwitchTests for #233).
budget rss=800 stalls50=20
pace 0.5
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=one
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://navigate?url=${PAGE}?n=two
expect-log GET /page.html\?n=two
wait 1.5
cra://debug?back=start
expect-log back start: selected=\S+n=two back=1

# ⌥← typed on the keyboard: left for the page; the tab stays where it is.
cra://debug?key=,123,524288&source=keyboard
expect-log mouse key back: left for the page, typed on the keyboard
wait 1.5
cra://debug?back=kept
expect-log back kept: selected=\S+n=two back=1

# ⌥← posted by another app (a mouse's side button through its driver): back, as #233 has it. A background test copy
# has no key window, so it says so instead of going back.
cra://debug?key=,123,524288
expect-log mouse key back: history
